      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The choice to step away when things become unbearable is a very human form of self-preservation, and you deserve to protect yourself from further pain. That urge to opt out before the suffering peaks is a signal that your internal reserves are completely depleted. It might be time to stop trying to manage the wreckage and instead focus entirely on finding a quiet, safe exit for *yourself*. Don't feel obligated to witness the final, ugly moments of something that has already failed.",
